### Rationale
E1 tested the launch path and found it can be tuned well below cluster-2. On an **empty** kernel, any cluster attribute removes about 0.25 µs, even a cluster of size 1 (1.69 → 1.44 µs). Cluster 16 removes about 0.38 µs. A 150 µs CPU delay still saves a further 0.29 µs on top of a clustered launch. So the H19 penalty exists without memory traffic, and it is a separate effect from the cluster gain.

On the real kernel body, two configurations win, each in its own size range:
- **Cluster 16 + cooperative:** 0.14–0.22 µs faster than cluster-2 at n ≤ 40960.
- **Cluster dim 1 + cooperative:** 0.18–0.23 µs faster at 163840–786432.

The candidate picks between them by n only. Grids above 1184 CTAs still use a plain launch. All 16 workloads pass run_tests. Against cluster-2 on the same GPU it is 7.9% faster at S, 5.2% faster at M and unchanged at L, so the success criterion is met and H15 is supported. The predicted score is 0.528, against 0.517 for the current best.

